{"content":[{"c":["ZOAR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of the “cities of the plain” confederate with Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboiim (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.2,8","r":"Gen.14.2,8","rawR":"Gen.14.2,8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.2,8","value":"Gen.14.2,8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:2, 8"},"). Zoar, also known by its earlier name Bela, is best known as the town that served as a temporary refuge for Lot and his daughters during the destruction of Sodom and the other cities of the plain (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.19.22-23,30","r":"Gen.19.22-23,30","rawR":"Gen.19.22-23,30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.19.22-23,30","value":"Gen.19.22-23,30"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:22-23, 30"},"). Despite the fact that Zoar was evidently a small town (v ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.19.22","r":"Gen.19.22","rawR":"Gen.19.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.19.22","value":"Gen.19.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"22"},"; Zoar means “little”), this place was evidently considered a significant geographical landmark in ancient times. When Abraham and Lot divided the land, Lot selected the land close to Zoar (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.13.10","r":"Gen.13.10","rawR":"Gen.13.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.13.10","value":"Gen.13.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:10"},"). When Moses surveyed the Promised Land from Mt Pisgah, Zoar was reckoned as the southern terminus of the plain of the valley of Jericho (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.34.3","r":"Deut.34.3","rawR":"Deut.34.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.34.3","value":"Deut.34.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 34:3"},"). During the prophetic period, Zoar was evidently considered to be on the southern boundary of Moab (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.15.5","r":"Isa.15.5","rawR":"Isa.15.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.15.5","value":"Isa.15.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 15:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.48.4,34","r":"Jer.48.4,34","rawR":"Jer.48.4,34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.48.4,34","value":"Jer.48.4,34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 48:4, 34"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CitiesofthePlain_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CitiesofthePlain_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CitiesofthePlain_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Cities of the Plain"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Zoar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 14:2, 8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.2,8","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.2,8","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.2,8"},{"anchorText":"19:22-23, 30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.19.22-23,30","rawQueryValue":"Gen.19.22-23,30","sourceRefExact":"Gen.19.22-23,30"},{"anchorText":"22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.19.22","rawQueryValue":"Gen.19.22","sourceRefExact":"Gen.19.22"},{"anchorText":"13:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.13.10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.13.10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.13.10"},{"anchorText":"Dt 34:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.34.3","rawQueryValue":"Deut.34.3","sourceRefExact":"Deut.34.3"},{"anchorText":"Is 15:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.15.5","rawQueryValue":"Isa.15.5","sourceRefExact":"Isa.15.5"},{"anchorText":"Jer 48:4, 34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.48.4,34","rawQueryValue":"Jer.48.4,34","sourceRefExact":"Jer.48.4,34"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"312792477b5da2d782d33200ec563cf6a4dccc7e1a12785fa388b619b881c388","sourceItemName":"Zoar","sourceItemOrder":143,"sourceMember":"Articles/Z.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Zoar","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Zoar","title":"Zoar","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}